---
title: PB&J Creme Pie Cookies
image: https://marisabakes.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/PB-J-Cookie-Sandwiches20805.jpg
author: Jesse Szewczyk
servings: 15
tags: gluten-free, peanut butter
---

> The source is just a repost of Cookies by Jesse Szewczyk. 

Preheat the oven to 350°F.

Line 2 #baking sheets{} with parchment paper.

In a #large bowl{}, combine @eggs{2}, @vanilla{1%tbsp}, @brown sugar{4/3%cups}, @sugar{1/2%cup}. Whisk until smooth, pale yellow, and slightly ribbony.

Add @peanut butter{2%cups}(smooth), @baking soda{2%tsp}, and @salt{1%tsp} and stir with a rubber spatula until a thick, smooth dough forms. It should be like Play-Doh.

Place @sugar{1/2%cup} on a plate.

Portion the dough into about 2 tablespoon balls. Roll the balls in the sugar and place at least 3 inches apart on the cookie sheets.

Press the dough balls down with the palm of your hand, to about 1/2 inch thick.

Bake both sheets at the same time, swapping midway, until the tops begin to crack, about ~{9-11%minutes}.

== Filling ==

In a #stand mixer{} with the paddle attachment, combine @butter{1%stick}(unsalted, softened), @peanut butter{1/2%cup}(smooth), @vanilla{1%tsp}, and @salt{1%pinch}.

With the mixer running on low speed, slowly add @confectioners' sugar{2%cups} until incorporated ~{3-4%minutes}.

Increase the mixer speed to medium-high and whip until fluffy, ~{1-2%minutes}.

Carefully flip over half the cookies.

Dollop about 2 tablespoons of the filling onto the the flipped cookies. 

Put some @strawberry jam{3/4%cup} on top of each dollop, around 2 teaspoon per cookie. 

Put the unflipped cookies on top of the jelly and press very lightly.

Let sit uncovered at room temperature for ~{2%hours} to let the filling firm up.

These tend to be a little dense, so I recommend cutting them in half with a knife carefully, cleaning the knife between cuts.

Keep refrigerated.